$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Dibarrelane-1-carboxylic Acid (9). To a solution of HgCl2 (330 mg, 1.22
mmol) in H2O (24 mL) was added Zn powder (12.0 g, 184 mmol), and the
mixture was vigorously stirred for 1 h. The supernatant liquid was
removed by decantation. To the residue were added concentrated HCl (60
mL), H2O (40 mL), and a solution of diketone 15 (559 mg, 2.02 mmol) in
toluene (14 mL), and the twophase mixture was vigorously stirred and
heated to reflux. Zn powder (9.0 g) was added portionwise until products
converged on a single spot by TLC analysis. After it was cooled to room
temperature, the mixture was diluted with Et2O/H2O and separated. The
aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were
washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by silica gel chromatography with
hexane/EtOAc (5/1). 9 (269 mg, 61% yield) as a colorless solid. R f =
0.38 (hexane/EtOAc 2/1); mp 144-145 °C (from CH2Cl2/hexane); 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.10 (dddd, J = 13.3, 10.8, 1.4, 1.4 Hz, 2H), 1.89 (ddddd,
J = 13.3, 10.8, 2.9, 1.4, 1.4 Hz, 2H), 1.73-1.58 (m, 5H), 1.53-1.44 (m,
4H), 1.33-1.22 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 185.0, 41.1, 39.5,
37.5, 31.8, 30.7, 30.3, 28.7, 28.0, 26.6, 26.4; IR (ATR) 2925, 2855,
2654, 1686, 1458, 1412, 1282, 952 cm-1; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calcd for
C14H20NaO2 243.1355, found 243.1350. Crystal data and structure
refinement: Identification code: biscooh; Empirical formula: C14 H20 O2;
Formula weight: 220.30; Temperature: 173 K; Wavelength: 0.71073 Å;
Crystal system: Monoclinic; Space group: P2(1)/c; Unit cell dimensions: a
= 6.7640(11) Å α= 90°. b = 10.5710(17) Å β= 93.658(2) °. c = 15.916(3) Å
γ = 90°. Volume: 1135.7(3) Å3; Z: 4; Density (calculated): 1.288 Mg/m3;
Absorption coefficient: 0.084 mm-1; F(000): 480; Crystal size: 0.57 x
0.34 x 0.32 mm3; Theta range for data collection: 2.31 to 27.60 °. Index
ranges: -7<=h<=8, -9<=k<=13, -20<=l<=20; Reflections collected: 6005;
Independent reflections: 2560 [R(int) = 0.1088]; Completeness to theta =
25.00°: 99.4 %; Absorption correction: Analytical; Max. and min.
transmission: 0.9737 and 0.8794; Refinement method: Full-matrix
least-squares on F2; Data / restraints / parameters: 2560 / 0 / 146;
Goodness-of-fit on F2: 1.045; Final R indices [I>2sigma(I)]: R1 = 0.0639,
wR2 = 0.1699; R indices (all data): R1 = 0.0671, wR2 = 0.1735; Largest
diff. peak and hole: 0.379 and -0.489 e Å-3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Clemmensen reduction; supernatant liquid obtained after stage 1 removed
by decantation and residue used in stage 2; portionwise addition of Zn
powder (stage 3)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Dibarrelane, a Dibicyclo[2.2.2]octane Hydrocarbon
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Suzuki, Takahiro; Okuyama, Hiroshi; Takano, Atsuhiro; Suzuki, Shinya;
Shimizu, Isao; Kobayashi, Susumu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(6), 2803-2808

